    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Provider configuration",
      "items": [
        "endpoint, auth_url, client_id, client_secret and scopes, or the LAKEKEEPER_* environment variables",
        "cacert_file and insecure set up TLS for every request",
        "Configure builds one *api.Client and hands it to every resource and data source"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Layer rule",
      "items": [
        "Only internal/provider/api imports the Lakekeeper Go SDK",
        "A depguard rule in .golangci.yml enforces it",
        "A missing endpoint becomes a new *api.Client method"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authentication",
      "items": [
        "OAuth 2.0 client credentials grant against auth_url",
        "The token source is set up in api/config.go; the SDK fetches and refreshes the token",
        "Each REST call carries the token as a bearer token"
      ]
    }
